.TH RYZENPROFILE "1" "February 2026" "ryzenprofile v1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ryzenprofile \- manual page for ryzenprofile v1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ryzenprofile
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
[info*]: Init system: 'runit'
.PP
Desc: Create, update, and manage init (runit) service that applies a Ryzen power profile at boot
.IP
using ryzenadj (AMD CPU only).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-apply\fR
Restart the init (runit) service (apply power profile immediately)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-install\fR
Install runit service and daemon script
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-uninstall\fR
Uninstall the runit service
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR
List available profiles and currently active profile
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR
Show running workers
.TP
\fB\-\-kill\-stale\fR
Kill stale workers
.TP
\fB\-\-custom\-args=\fR""
Pass additional ryzenadj flags
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-generate\-profiles\fR
Generate all profiles defined in CONFIG: '/etc/ryzenprofile/config'
\-> generated profiles written to '/etc/ryzenprofile/profiles/*'
.IP
(Will use live or cached stock limits)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-service\-name\fR=\fI\,NAME\/\fR
Service name (default: 'ryzenprofile')
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-worker\-name\fR=\fI\,NAME\/\fR
New worker instances name (default: 'RyzenProfile')
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-set\fR
Set a profile in (\fI\,/etc/ryzenprofile/config\/\fP), conjunction with \fB\-p\fR
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR=\fI\,PROFILE\/\fR
Predefined profile for runit system (default: balanced):
extreme_save, ultra_save, powersave, eco,
balanced_low, balanced, stock, performance
or 'custom'
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-ryzenadj\-path\fR=\fI\,PATH\/\fR
Path to ryzenadj binary (default: \fI\,/usr/bin/ryzenadj\/\fP)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR
Check if the runit service exists and is enabled
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose mode
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
ryzenprofile \-s \-p performance
# Set profile to 'performance'
.TP
ryzenprofile \-\-init \-\-install
# Install and configure in one command
.TP
ryzenprofile \-u
# Uninstall service
.IP
# Set additional ryzenadj args for profile 'performance'
ryzenprofile \-s \-p performance  \-\-custom\-args="\-\-max\-performance"
.SS "Available profiles (under '/etc/ryzenprofile/profiles/*'):"
.IP
balanced gaming light max performance powersave silent stock ultra_powersave
